        "original_id": "e0e3a8a0-e20e-5873-bebd-66f4ca2fa602",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Programs: California Healthy Families Program, Children's Health Insurance Program\n- Organizations: United States Department of Health and Human Services\n- Places: California\n- Topics: children's health insurance, low-cost coverage, state implementation\n\nFacts:\n- The Children's Health Insurance Program, formerly known as the State Children's Health Insurance Program, is administered by the United States Department of Health and Human Services.\n- The Children's Health Insurance Program provides matching funds to states for health insurance for families with children.\n- The California Healthy Families Program is California's implementation of the federal Children's Health Insurance Program.\n- The California Healthy Families Program provides low-cost health, dental, and vision insurance to children who currently lack insurance and do not qualify for no-cost Medi-Cal.",
